# Origin mode (DECOM): positions counted from the scrolling region.

test setting origin mode moves the cursor to the home of the region
spec VT100 User Guide DECOM: the cursor is moved to the new home position when the mode is set
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[4;5H\e[?6h
cursor 2,1

test resetting origin mode moves the cursor to the home of the screen
spec VT100 User Guide DECOM: the cursor is moved to the new home position when the mode is reset
known-fail: alacritty – resetting DECOM leaves the cursor where it is
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[?6h\e[3;3H\e[?6l
cursor 1,1

test CUP counts from the top of the region
spec VT100 User Guide DECOM: line numbers are relative to the margin settings
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[?6h\e[1;1Hx\e[2;3Hy
screen
||
|x|
|  y|

test HVP counts from the top of the region
spec VT100 User Guide DECOM: CUP and HVP are relative in origin mode
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[?6h\e[2;2fx
screen
||
||
| x|

test the cursor cannot leave the region in origin mode
spec VT100 User Guide DECOM: the cursor is not allowed to be positioned outside the margins
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[?6h\e[9;9H
cursor 4,9

test VPA counts from the top of the region
spec VT100 User Guide DECOM: line numbers are relative; xterm ctlseqs CSI Ps d
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[?6h\e[2d
cursor 3,1

test CPR is relative to the region
spec VT100 User Guide CPR: the numbering of lines depends on the state of origin mode
known-fail: alacritty – CPR reports the absolute row while origin mode is set
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[?6h\e[2;3H\e[6n
reply \e[2;3R

test DECSTBM in origin mode puts the cursor at the new home
spec VT100 User Guide DECSTBM: the cursor is placed in the home position (see DECOM)
size 10 5
feed \e[?6h\e[3;5r
cursor 3,1

test CUP is absolute when origin mode is off
spec VT100 User Guide DECOM: the cursor may be positioned outside the margins
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[1;1Hx\e[5;1Hy
screen
|x|
||
||
||
|y|

test origin mode survives a scroll
convention origin mode is a mode, not a position
size 10 5
feed \e[2;3r\e[?6h\e[2;1H\n\n\e[1;1Hz
screen
||
|z|

test a soft reset ends origin mode
spec VT510 DECSTR Table 5-9: origin mode absolute
known-fail: alacritty – DECSTR (CSI ! p) is not implemented
size 10 5
feed \e[2;4r\e[?6h\e[!p\e[1;1Hx
screen
|x|

test DECSTBM with only a top margin in origin mode puts the cursor at the top of the region
spec VT510 DECSTBM: the bottom margin defaults to the last line, and the cursor goes to the home position, which DECOM puts at the top margin
size 10 5
feed \e[?6h\e[3r
cursor 3,1
